It should be kept in mind that the following will capture every comment which is surrounded by "@@@". If you want to capture only one line assertions, replace "\r?\n" with ".". The regex "@@.+\r?\n" will match "@@@" and everything until the new line.


Here is the corresponding code in C# to capture the assert statements:

```Csharp
using System;
using System.Text.RegularExpressions;

class Program
{
    private static void Main()
    {
        string code = @"<paste your code from QA>";  // paste the code here
        string[] matches = Regex.Split(code, @"(?<=@@|[\n])");

        foreach (var match in matches)
        {
            if (match.StartsWith("Debug.Assert("))
            {
                 Console.WriteLine(match.Trim());
            }
        }
    }
}
```
